PianoDwc3 is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). What it takes from other work, and from where:

Project-SunUEFI 4ef87402e9d58465af871e4c4f4a5de87599d81c (unixnu-research/Project-SunUEFI; files BSD-2-Clause-Patent)
  uefi/core/PianoDwc3Device.c  piano-measured DWC3 takeover order and values: PHY interfaces woken before DCTL.CSFTRST, the
                               DWC_usb31/32 reset timing (20 ms steps, 200 ms, 50 ms settle), GCTL device | DSBLCLKGTNG,
                               DCFG NUMP 16, DEPSTARTCFG + one transfer resource per endpoint, the QSCRATCH session override
                               (0x0A6F8810 | 0x10100000, 0x0A6F8830 | 0x01000000) before RUN_STOP, DCFG.DevAddr written in the
                               SETUP stage of SET_ADDRESS, END TRANSFER with ForceRM and the 1 ms wait. Re-implemented, not copied.
  uefi/core/PianoUsbPhy.c      the M31 eUSB2 PHY init writes (PianoUsbHw.h kM31Init, piano-usb-phy=1) and the byte-wide
                               register note; the order of the PHY reset.
  docs/archive/storage-usb/usb-link-audit.md   the piano measurements cited in docs/drivers/usb-device-debug.md.

QcomDwc3 e4efe95c903a737e0f5955e5b50a8fb4d2a7d718 (unixnu-research/QcomDwc3)
  QcomDwc3.cpp (BSD-2-Clause-Patent): the SPMI v7 observer-read pattern for the eUSB2 repeater (SID 7, 0xfd), the GDSC enable
  shape (SW_COLLAPSE off, RETAIN_FF on), the coherence note (bypass leaves the master non-coherent). Re-implemented.
  NOT used: QcomEusb2Phy.h, QcomQmpUsb3.h (GPL-2.0-only), and its AppleUSBXDCI/AppleUSBXHCI subclasses (no such classes in the
  macOS 27.0.1 VM kernel collection).

UniXNU-sm8750-common feaa135df4763e3c19a155402e6b17b124a12e13 kits/Sm8750Platform/SmmuTakeover.h (BSD-2-Clause-Patent)
  SmmuStream.h follows its bypass-bank shape (SCTLR 0, CBA2R VA64, CBAR 0x10000), its geometry checks and the global TLB sync
  with a non-zero value. Written anew for SID 0x40 (redirect/keep of an existing exact entry, no panic).

The cold start (UsbCold.h, piano-usb-cold, 2026-11-12):
  Specifications only (GPL-2.0, register facts and the order of steps; no code or text copied): the Ubuntu piano kernel's
  drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c (status 0x08 b7, EN_CTL1 0x46 b7, FORCE_EN_5 0xe8 / FORCE_VAL_5 0xed b6, the tuning
  registers 0x50..0x5b and which DT property sets which, the squelch scale; enable, then tuning, then the status poll; device mode
  clears the forced clock), phy-qcom-m31-eusb2.c (the M31 bit names; rails, then the repeater, then the reference clock, then the PHY
  reset, then its tables), drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c (the glue's block reset at probe), drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c and clk-rcg2.c
  (GDSC and RCG bits), drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c (offsets, GPLL0's vote word 0x52020, the USB30 GDSC's waits).
  The tables are this repository's: the M31 init (kM31Init, Project-SunUEFI's stock sequence, above), the repeater tuning and the
  rails (names, ranges, PMICs) from piano's boot DT (board facts; the same on every unit, no calibration).
  Reused from this repository (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, included, not copied): package/PianoBluetooth/BtRpmh.h (vrmSend: one VRM
  transaction on apps DRV-2), package/PianoKeyboard/CmdDb.h (the cmd-db lookup, the RSC layout), package/PianoPower/ChargerPmic.h and
  SpmiObserver.h (the PMIC's Type-C block found and read), the lock-word protocol of PianoA830's Sm8750GpuPower.c / Sm8750Rpmh.h
  (sm8750_gcc_vote_owner, sm8750_rpmh_drv2_owner: imported from PianoA830, not defined here), the LDO page rule of
  package/include/PianoWcnRails.h.

Specifications only (no code or text copied): mainline Linux drivers/usb/dwc3 (core.h, gadget.c, ep0.c, dwc3-qcom.c),
drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c and tcsrcc-sm8750.c (register offsets), the piano DT (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb), the USB 2.0,
IAD and CDC 1.2 / PSTN specifications, ARM IHI 0062 (SMMUv2). Mu-Silicium's SamsungPkg UsbfnDwc3Dxe (Linux-derived) was not read.

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent, for the HID input (piano-usb-hid=1):
  package/PianoKeyboard/HidDescriptors.h and Wn8030Piano.h: included as they are (build -I package/PianoKeyboard), not copied: the
  keyboard (+ consumer) and pointer report descriptors the PianoUsbHID devices declare, and the report sizes/IDs HidInput.h's reports
  are checked against (tests/hid_input_host.cpp, static_asserts and a descriptor walk).
  package/PianoInput/PianoInput.cpp, package/PianoKeyboard/PianoKeyboard.cpp: the IOHIDDevice subclass pattern (provenance: their
  UPSTREAM): the same overrides, OSTypeAlloc/init/Built-In/attach/start under the driver's service from
  start(), handleReport from a kernel thread, the IOHIDEventService publish notification, the codeless IOHIDEventDriver personality
  and the 334-slot vtable check in the kext descriptor. Re-written for PianoUsbHID (own product ID 0x5055 and names).

The network function (piano-usb-net=1):
  Ncm.h, the NCM parts of UsbDescriptors.h and Dwc3Gadget.h: written from the public USB CDC NCM 1.0 (NTH16/NDP16, alignment, the
  NTB parameters, the requests and notifications, alternate settings) and CDC ECM 1.2 (the Ethernet networking functional
  descriptor) specifications. Linux's drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c and u_ether.c (GPL-2.0) were not copied or used as
  text; nothing of them is in this package.
  TxFifoPlan.h: the DWC3 TX FIFO rules (GTXFIFOSIZn layout, k packets = k * (MaxPacket/word + 1) + 1 words, RAM1 / single-port RAM0
  depth, MDWIDTH) from the controller's programming model as mainline Linux drivers/usb/dwc3 (core.h, gadget.c TX FIFO resizing)
  describes it: specification only, as above. The numbers are piano's, from the T1 probe.
  PianoUsbNet.cpp: this repository's package/PianoNullEthernet (its IOEthernetController pattern; provenance: its UPSTREAM):
  the same overrides and __PRIVATE_SPI__ include, no output queue with outputPacket under a lock, inputPacket from one thread
  (the source's receive loop), the 400-slot vtable check. Re-written: not built-in, link from the USB side, own work loop,
  own MAC.
